@startuml sample_format
!theme cyborg
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam backgroundColor #0b1018
skinparam defaultFontColor #e6edf7
skinparam ArrowColor #a9b8ca
skinparam ArrowFontColor #e6edf7
skinparam rectangle {
 BackgroundColor #273241
 BorderColor #61738a
 FontColor #e6edf7
}
skinparam note {
 BackgroundColor #1b2533
 BorderColor #61738a
 FontColor #e6edf7
}
title Sample bits in a 32-bit slot and the mono channel mapping (design, not implemented)
top to bottom direction
rectangle "**RX frame from the INMP441** (i2s0, L/R pin to ground)\n\n<#273241,#61738a>|= Left slot, 32 bits |= Right slot, 32 bits |\n| <#10302b> bits 31…8: 24-bit sample, two's complement, MSB first | <#2a1714> not driven by the microphone |\n| <#2a1714> bits 7…0: not driven after the LSB | <#2a1714> ignored by the loop |" as receiveFrame
rectangle "**Mono working sample** (int32, one per frame, 64 per block)\n\n<#273241,#61738a>|= bits 31…8 |= bits 7…0 |\n| <#10302b> 24-bit sample, left-aligned | cleared to 0 |" as monoSample
rectangle "**Processing step**\nthis step: copy, sample unchanged\nlater: listening filter and volume" as processing
rectangle "**TX frame to the PCM5102A** (i2s1, 32-bit words)\n\n<#273241,#61738a>|= Left slot, 32 bits |= Right slot, 32 bits |\n| <#10302b> mono sample | <#10302b> same mono sample |" as transmitFrame
receiveFrame --> monoSample : take the left slot (even index),\nclear bits 7…0
monoSample --> processing
processing --> transmitFrame : write the result into both slots
note right of monoSample
  Left-aligned keeps the full 32-bit DAC scale,
  so the copy step needs no shift
  (decision of 11 November).
  Not chosen: signed 24-bit, right-aligned,
  which needs an 8-bit shift into the TX slot.
end note
legend bottom
  Bit layout: INMP441 datasheet, section "I²S Data Interface" and Figure 9 (mono, left channel).
  Both DAC channels carry the same sample; audible output is not verified yet (bring-up T09 not run).
endlegend
@enduml
